="epo"><addressbook><name>SAIJO KINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYO KOHAN CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHSAWA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAIJO, KINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYO KOHAN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHSAWA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAIJO KINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHSAWA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAIJO, KINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of manufacturing a multilayered printed-circuit board and a low-cost clad board. Copper foil layers (19, 24, 33) for forming conductor layers (10, 17, 18) and nickel plating layers (20, 21) for forming etch stop layers (11, 12) are alternately stacked and compressed to form a clad board (34) for a printed-circuit board. The clad board (34) for the printed-circuit board is selectively etched to manufacture a base. External conductor layers (15, 16) are formed on the surface of the base and patterned. The conductor layers (10, 15, 16) are interconnected electrically through conductors blocks (17, 18) formed by etching the copper foil layers (19, 24, 33) and the nickel plating layers (20, 21) to complete the manufacture of multilayered printed-circuit board.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un procédé de fabrication d'une carte à circuit imprimé et d'une carte plaquée de faible coût, selon lequel on empile en alternance et on comprime des couches de feuilles de cuivre (19, 24, 33) qui formeront les couches de conducteurs (10, 17, 18) et des couches nickelées (20, 21) qui formeront les couches d'arrêt d'attaque (11, 12) afin d'obtenir une carte plaquée (34) pour carte à circuit imprimé. On fabrique un substrat en gravant sélectivement la carte plaquée (34) pour carte à circuit imprimé. On forme ensuite des réseaux de couches de conducteurs externes (15, 16) sur la surface du substrat. Pour achever la fabrication de la carte à circuit imprimé multicouche, on relie électriquement les couches de conducteurs (10, 15, 16) via des blocs conducteurs (17, 18) que l'on forme en gravant les couches de feuilles de cuivre (19, 24, 33) et les couches nickelées (20, 21).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>